    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2610.11111v2</id>
    <title>Tightly Coupled LiDAR-Inertial Odometry
      with Loop Closure for UAVs</title>
    <updated>2026-10-17T09:00:00Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.11111v2" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2610.11111v2" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>We present a LiDAR-inertial odometry system for UAVs that adds loop closure and pose graph
      optimisation to a tightly coupled filter. On public datasets it reduces drift compared with
      FAST-LIO2. Code: https://github.com/example/lio-uav.</summary>
    <category term="cs.RO" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2026-10-15T17:00:00Z</published>
    <arxiv:comment>Accepted to IROS 2026. 8 pages, 6 figures</arxiv:comment>
    <arxiv:primary_category term="cs.RO"/>
    <author><name>Ada Lovelace</name></author>
    <author><name>Alan Turing</name></author>
  </entry>
