    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2610.22222v1</id>
    <title>Steering $\pi_0$: Action Chunking for Bimanual Cloth Folding</title>
    <updated>2026-10-16T08:00:00Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.22222v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2610.22222v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <link title="doi" href="https://doi.org/10.1234/ABC.5678" rel="related"/>
    <summary>Vision-language-action models such as $\pi_0$ struggle with deformable objects. We study
      action chunking for bimanual cloth folding on a low-cost SO-101 setup with imitation learning.</summary>
    <category term="cs.RO" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
